# The checks pattern 32 closed: an assertion about a set (T12.7, REQ-SELF-2).
#
# Nineteen rows of the Phase 11 parity report said the same thing in different
# words — "the language asserts about one element, not about a set" — and
# Draft 2.15 gave the language the sentence. This file is what that sentence
# bought: every story here is the Yam side of a check that had only the
# Playwright one, and the check ids in `checks.yaml` pair them.
#
# ## Why the scope is named
#
# `Every row of the named requests table` names the table, and the table's
# binding is an `automationId` like every other. A sentence scoped to `this
# screen` reads the whole window, which is right for "no secret is anywhere"
# and wrong for "every row of a table" — the second would sweep the rail, the
# toolbar and the inspector too, and pass or fail for reasons nobody wrote down.
#
# ## Why an empty set fails
#
# It is the executor's rule, not this file's (LLD §13.9): a screen that has not
# finished loading has no rows, and "every row is visible" over none of them is
# true. So each story clicks its way to the screen and asserts one control it
# owns *before* it asserts about a set — the same order a person reads in.
#
# ## The project is opened by the first story
#
# A flow owns one session on its adapter (REQ-RUN-3), so each file arrives at an
# ADE that is showing whatever the last one left — and the Recent list is what
# opens a project, exactly as `02-ade-screen.flow` does it. Only the first story
# here does it; every story after it is on a window that already has one, which
# is the arrangement `01-ade-screens.flow` uses too.
#
# ## The number in the file name
#
# `yam run` executes a project's `test:` blocks in file order and one session
# serves the whole run, so `99-` — the flow that quits — stays last.

story: every interactive control on the Flows screen is named and id'd
  The first recent project should be visible
  Click the first recent project
  The Flows rail item should be visible
  Click the Flows rail item
  The Flows heading should be visible
  Every control on this screen should have a name
  Every control on this screen should have an id

story: the Data screen names every secret and shows none of them
  Click the Data rail item
  The Save data button should be visible
  The run data table should contain "YAM_SAMPLE_PASSWORD"
  No text on this screen should contain {data.injected.password}

story: the Settings screen shows the project and never a credential
  Click the Settings rail item
  The project settings table should contain "yam-fixtures"
  The run settings table should contain "playwright"
  The diagnostics panel should be visible
  No text on this screen should contain {data.injected.modelKey}

story: the Agents screen lists what an agent may call
  Click the Agents and tools rail item
  The exposed tools table should be visible
  The invocations table should be visible
  The refused panel should be visible
  Every row of the exposed tools table should be visible

story: the API screen shows a saved request and its headers
  Click the API rail item
  The named requests table should be visible
  The named requests table should contain "active count"
  The request pane should be visible
  Every row of the named requests table should be visible

story: the Import screen previews into the open project and nowhere else
  Click the Import prototype database rail item
  The prototype database field should be visible
  The where it may write panel should contain "anything outside it"
  The terminal panel should contain "yam migrate"

story: the Bindings screen shows the store and one element's resolver order
  Click the Bindings rail item
  The bindings table should be visible
  Every row of the bindings table should be visible
  Click the Verify all bindings button

story: the legacy screens are gone
  Click the Flows rail item
  The Flows heading should be visible
  No control on this screen should have the "id" attribute "rail-legacy"
  No element on this screen should have the "id" attribute "screen-project"
  No element on this screen should have the "id" attribute "screen-plan"
  No element on this screen should have the "id" attribute "screen-results"
  No element on this screen should have the "id" attribute "screen-tools"

test: the ADE's sets
  every interactive control on the Flows screen is named and id'd
  the Data screen names every secret and shows none of them
  the Settings screen shows the project and never a credential
  the Agents screen lists what an agent may call
  the API screen shows a saved request and its headers
  the Import screen previews into the open project and nowhere else
  the Bindings screen shows the store and one element's resolver order
  the legacy screens are gone
